# Flintroom backend configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Every name below is a field on `Settings` in
# `app/core/config.py`, which is the authority — this file is a map of it, not a
# second source of truth. If the two disagree, config.py is right.
#
# `extra="ignore"` means a name NOT on that class is accepted and silently does
# nothing. That is how `ELEVENLABS_AGENT_ID` (retired with ElevenLabs Agents in
# #38) and `OPENAI_API_KEY` (never in this stack) can sit in a real `.env`
# looking load-bearing. If you add a line here and nothing changes, check the
# spelling against config.py before assuming the code is wrong.
#
# THREE FAILURE MODES, and knowing which is which saves an afternoon:
#   - REQUIRED below means the process refuses to boot. Loud, immediate.
#   - A missing optional key usually disables one feature and answers 502 on the
#     endpoints that need it. Everything else keeps working — that is deliberate
#     (see `build_object_storage`), and it is why a whole subsystem can be dark
#     without anything looking broken.
#   - A key with a default is silently fine. Leave it alone unless you mean it.


# --- REQUIRED: the process will not start without these -------------------

# No default on purpose. A process that boots without a database and finds out
# on the first sweep looks healthy to every deploy check while billing nobody.
# The driver is part of the URL and must be `asyncpg` — everything is async.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://flintroom:flintroom@localhost:55432/flintroom_dev

# Signs our own access tokens. Minimum 32 bytes, enforced — RFC 7518's floor for
# HMAC-SHA256, below which the key is weaker than the hash and brute-forceable
# offline by anyone holding one token. No default, because a signing key that
# falls back to a literal is a key that ships, and then every deployment that
# forgot to set one can forge tokens for every other.
#   openssl rand -base64 48
JWT_SECRET=

# The `aud` values `OidcVerifier` pins. Pinning is what stops a genuine Google
# token minted for somebody else's app signing in here.
#
# COMMA-SEPARATED, and you will usually need more than one for Google: the
# native Android SDK asks with the WEB client, iOS asks with its own, and a
# token carries exactly one `aud`. A single pinned value cannot serve both, and
# the failure is a 401 that names nothing — `sign_in` refuses to say which check
# failed. Widening the set does not weaken it; every value is a client in our
# own project.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
APPLE_CLIENT_ID=


# --- Object storage: attached decks and saved rooms -----------------------
#
# Absent, `build_object_storage` returns None at boot and EVERY ingestion
# endpoint answers 502 `provider_unavailable`. Nothing else is affected — auth,
# balances and the voice loop all work without a bucket, which is why refusing
# to start over it would be the wrong trade. It is also why this is easy to miss
# for a day: the app just says it cannot read your attached material.
#
# The values below are the MinIO in `docker-compose.yml`. `docker compose up`
# creates the bucket; nothing in application code does, because a process that
# can create buckets holds more S3 permission than it needs for the rest of its
# life. Production swaps the endpoint and the credential pair — R2, S3 and B2
# all speak the same API here.
S3_ENDPOINT_URL=http://localhost:59000
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=flintroom
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=flintroom
S3_BUCKET=flintroom-material

# Where the bucket name goes: in the hostname (`virtual`) or in the path.
# Defaults to `virtual`, which is right for AWS. MinIO has no DNS to put a
# bucket in front of, and Cloudflare R2 documents `path` too.
S3_ADDRESSING_STYLE=path

# SigV4 signs over a region whether or not the store has one. MinIO accepts any
# value; S3 does not. Default `us-east-1`.
#S3_REGION=us-east-1


# --- Voice: the live interrogation ----------------------------------------
#
# Without the key there is no room. Speech and transcription both hang off it.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# Fallback voice for an archetype that has not been given one.
#ELEVENLABS_DEFAULT_VOICE_ID=

# How long a silence ends the presenter's turn. Unset uses the provider's own.
#VAD_SILENCE_THRESHOLD_SECS=

# Pin the transcriber to one language instead of letting it detect. Unset
# detects.
#TRANSCRIPTION_LANGUAGE=

# Defaults are current and deliberate — `docs/voice-cost.md` before changing
# either, since the synthesis model is where the room's bill actually goes.
#SPEECH_MODEL=eleven_flash_v2_5
#EXPRESSIVE_SPEECH_MODEL=eleven_v3


# --- Models: the panel, the Auditor, extraction, the coach ----------------
#
# The panel is Gemini; extraction and the debrief can be either. A provider set
# to a vendor whose key is absent is a 502 on that feature only.
#
# #13 is the open task measuring Claude against Gemini for the panel. Until it
# lands these defaults are a choice, not a finding.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Needed only if a provider below is set to `claude`. #61 records that ingestion
# ran on an Anthropic account that could not be funded — check that before
# switching.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

#EXTRACTION_PROVIDER=gemini
#DEBRIEF_PROVIDER=gemini
#PANEL_PROVIDER=gemini

#PANEL_COMPOSITION_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
#EXTRACTION_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash
#DEBRIEF_MODEL=gemini-3.7-flash
#COACH_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash


# --- Billing --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Verified BEFORE the payload is parsed. Unset, webhooks are rejected and
# audited rather than trusted — so purchases will not grant anything.
# `docs/billing-setup.md` is the console work that produces this.
#REVENUECAT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=


# --- Ingestion tuning -----------------------------------------------------
#
# Fine as they are. Listed so they are discoverable rather than folklore.

# Parallel extraction calls per material. 1-64.
#EXTRACTION_CONCURRENT_CALLS=4

# A backstop, unpublished on purpose — see `MONTHLY_PAGE_BUDGET` in
# `billing/tiers.py`. Unpublished means it can be tightened in a deploy; a
# figure on a tier card cannot.
#DAILY_PAGE_CEILING=600

# Converts PPTX for extraction. Must be on PATH.
#LIBREOFFICE_BINARY=soffice
